# Dependencies
**/node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
bun-debug.log*

# Build artifacts (keep for production, but we copy only what's needed)
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/

# Git
.git
.gitignore
**/.gitignore

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment files (should use runtime injection)
#
# The patterns below were enumerated one-by-one and so covered only the env files that existed
# when they were written. apps/web/Dockerfile does `COPY apps/web/ ./apps/web/`, so any env file
# NOT listed here lands in the builder layer — and apps/web/.env.e2e holds CLERK_SECRET_KEY,
# TEST_CLERK_PASSWORD and ENCRYPTION_KEY. It never reaches the final image (only dist is copied
# out), but a pushed or cached builder layer would carry it.
#
# `.env*` is a wildcard on purpose: the next .env.<something> a developer creates is covered
# without anyone remembering to come back here. The .example templates are re-admitted below
# because they are committed, contain only placeholders, and some builds read them.
.env*
**/.env*
!.env*.example
!**/.env*.example

# Local TLS material. `apps/web/.gitignore` ignores *.pem, but only under apps/web — a cert
# generated at the repo root or in backend/ would otherwise reach a build context.
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
*.p12
**/*.p12

# Testing artifacts
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/

# Documentation (not needed in container)
**/*.md
!config/**/*.md

# E2E tests (not needed in production image)
apps/web/e2e/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/test-results/

# Backend specific (when building frontend only)
backend/tmp/
backend/coverage/

# GitHub
.github/

# Plans and local dev files
.claude/plans/
